NEXT (human):
  1. Summarize the makeup dataset on its own:
       python -m harness.telemetry.summarize results/screening-batch1-makeup-w6
     It pairs with report/screening-batch1-makeup-w6/ (CLAUDE.md rule 8). Add the dataset row to
     results/README.md naming that report.
  2. Report W6 from THIS dataset only. Batch 1's W6 cells stay void; they are not re-graded, not back-filled and not merged in.
  3. Account for the 0 deferred-contaminated cell(s) and for any run the
     collector refused: both are HOLES, reported as missing, never averaged over.
  4. No number from this dataset enters docs, the site, or an external-facing
     report before CP-FINDINGS.

================================================================================
POST-PASS ADJUDICATION — 2026-08-21, written by the operator's agent, NOT by the
driver. THE PASS COMPLETED BUT IS NOT SCOREABLE AS AN OUTCOME MEASUREMENT.
Step 4 (the final summarize) was NOT run. Nothing here has entered any report.
================================================================================

WHAT THE PASS DID DELIVER
  15/15 runs executed, 0 skipped, 0 deferred, every run "validate: PASS
  (audit-grade)". Provider backfill under attribution rule v3: 9 legs
  backfilled, no contamination refusals. Known spend floor $12.2711 of a $150
  cap; 10 legs carry unavailable cost (never zero-filled).

  THE DELIVERY FIX WORKED. 14 of 15 runs produced a non-empty
  agent-solution.diff (batch 1: 0 of 15), and every one of those 14 diffs
  touches exactly one path, `review-report.txt`, and nothing else. The agents
  received `review-diff.patch`, read it, and wrote findings in the requested
  form. The void that made batch 1's W6 cells unscoreable did not recur.

WHY THE PASS IS STILL NOT A MEASUREMENT
  acceptance.result is `rejected` in 15 of 15 cells — including the 5 whose
  SEALED HIDDEN GATE PASSED (P0 rep1, rep2, rep3; C2 rep3; C3-med rep2). The
  outcome variable is again dominated by instrument error. Different mechanism
  from batch 1, same consequence: these verdicts measure the harness, not the
  agents. Two independent causes, both verified, neither speculative.

  D1 — THE GATE RAN FROM A STALE CONTAINER IMAGE.
    `lab-subject/w6-hono-router-review:3feb3551d46d` was built 2026-08-18
    07:10:45 UTC. Its baked gate scripts are dated Aug 17 and are missing BOTH
    fixes merged on 2026-08-20:
      - no `pr_review` block in its check-public.sh (PR #25), so review-report.txt
        is not in TARGET_PATHS;
      - no `git_trust_subject` in its lib.sh or check-hidden.sh (PR #24), i.e.
        the gate that graded these runs predates the git-ownership repair.
    Verified by running `grep` inside the image, not inferred from dates.

    ROOT CAUSE, and it is general — NOT specific to W6 or to this pass:
    harness/runner/run.py:1265 tags the gate image
    `subject_image_tag(task.task_id, task.pinned_commit)`, and `_ensure_image`
    builds only when that tag is absent locally. The tag is a function of the
    TASK and the SUBJECT COMMIT only; the harness and gate scripts baked into
    the image are not part of it. So any change to gate logic leaves the tag
    unchanged, the cached image is reused, and the OLD gate runs silently. Every
    task with a locally cached image is exposed to this.

    EFFECT HERE: P6-diff-scope fails in 14 of 15 cells — precisely the 14 that
    produced a review report. It "passes" only in C2 rep2, the one run that
    produced nothing. A gate that passes exactly the cell that did no work is
    the signature.

  D2 — THE LEAK SCAN REJECTS THE ARTIFACT THE HARNESS ITSELF DELIVERS.
    This one is NOT staleness. It is unfixed on main as of 21b7857.
    `leak_found()` (harness/task-tools/lib.sh) fails any subject tree containing
    a `*.patch` file anywhere outside the pruned dependency dirs. The W6
    delivery fix deliberately copies `review-diff.patch` INTO the subject tree —
    that is the whole point of the fix. Adding it to .git/info/exclude hides it
    from git (so it does not disturb P6) but not from `find`.
    Nothing in check-public.sh or lib.sh exempts the review_diff basename from
    the scan.
    EFFECT: P5-no-leakage fails in 15 of 15 cells, and WOULD STILL FAIL for
    every pr_review run after the image is rebuilt. Rebuilding alone does not
    make this task gradable; D2 needs a code fix and a regression test.

  A THIRD, CELL-LOCAL OBSERVATION (not an instrument defect):
    C2 rep2 ran 21:25:08 -> 21:45:14, hitting the 1200s agent bound
    (behavior.failures_by_category = {"claude_timeout": 1}) and produced a
    0-byte diff. Even after D1 and D2 are fixed, that cell is a truncated run —
    an instrument observation, not a capability one — and must be refused by any
    grader, exactly as batch 1's 17 truncated runs are.

WHAT IS AND IS NOT USABLE FROM THIS DATASET
  Usable: the telemetry. Token counts, timings, the v3 attribution and the cost
  floor are real, validated, and unaffected by D1/D2, which touch only grading.
  NOT usable: every acceptance verdict, and therefore any W6 outcome claim.
  This dataset is NOT merged with batch 1's void W6 cells and does not repair
  them. Batch 1's W6 cells stay void.

WHY NOTHING WAS RE-RUN
  Re-running is live model spend and needs a new CP-SPEND. Rebuilding the gate
  image and re-grading the 15 ARCHIVED agent-solution.diff files offline — the
  same zero-spend repair used on batch 1's 36 amended verdicts — may be possible
  for D1, but it cannot be done before D2 is fixed, and neither was authorized.
  Awaiting the human.
